{"journal_version":1,"sequence":9,"replace_from":13,"message_count":14,"messages":[{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"Verify passed. Let me check the sync public test to be sure it doesn't assert absence of a button on error... it passed. Also should I verify the error path manually? The task says do not modify tests. I could do a quick ad-hoc check, but budget limited. The implementation is straightforward. Let me quickly read the public sync test to confirm expectations (small read).\n\nActually a concern: the public test at line 51 only tests success path. Our error path: param is read once; retry always succeeds. Criterion \"Activating it immediately returns to Checking service…, then completes as All changes are synced.\" — yes.\n\nOne risk: repeated activation guard uses timerRef; on the error state timerRef is undefined (timer completed, set undefined). Good.\n\nAlso unmount cleanup — preserved.\n\nDone. Report.","content":"Verification passed. Summary of the change:\n\n**`src/components/AsyncPanel.tsx`**\n- Extracted the 120 ms simulated sync into a shared `schedule(next)` helper backed by a single `timerRef`, plus `clearTimer` for unmount cleanup (preserving the original cleanup behavior).\n- The mount effect still reads `?sync=` once and resolves to `error` or `success` exactly as before, so `/` is unchanged.\n- Added a `Retry sync` button inside the error alert. Its handler immediately sets `loading` and schedules the same 120 ms transition to `success`; it returns early if a timer is already pending, so repeated activation cannot create overlapping timers. The button renders only in the `error` state and so disappears on success. No navigation/reload or state reset — the selected task lives outside this component and `window.location` is never touched.\n\n**`src/styles.css`**\n- Added `.sync-retry { justify-self: start; margin-top: 8px; }` so the recovery action sits below the error copy, reusing the existing `button.secondary` style and existing focus-visible outline rules.\n\n**Commands actually run:** `verify_frontend` → `npm run build` (tsc + vite, success) and `npm run test:public` (Playwright, 6/6 passed). No existing tests were modified.\n\n**Remaining risks:** the retry path has no public test (only the success state does), so its behavior is verified by reasoning rather than an automated assertion; if a future test asserts a different delay constant, the shared `SYNC_DELAY` would be the single place to change. The guard relies on React's single-threaded click handling, which is adequate for this \"no overlapping timers\" requirement.","response_items":[{"id":"2c99e5e7-0250-4d47-8143-14ac01e315c8","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"Verify passed. Let me check the sync public test to be sure it doesn't assert absence of a button on error... it passed. Also should I verify the error path manually? The task says do not modify tests. I could do a quick ad-hoc check, but budget limited. The implementation is straightforward. Let me quickly read the public sync test to confirm expectations (small read).\n\nActually a concern: the public test at line 51 only tests success path. Our error path: param is read once; retry always succeeds. Criterion \"Activating it immediately returns to Checking service…, then completes as All changes are synced.\" — yes.\n\nOne risk: repeated activation guard uses timerRef; on the error state timerRef is undefined (timer completed, set undefined). Good.\n\nAlso unmount cleanup — preserved.\n\nDone. Report.","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":"8022a849-891b-458f-b235-74b6c76f8dbc-0","status":"completed"},{"id":"a533e7a5-798d-4427-a9b9-993e296b5492","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"Verification passed. Summary of the change:\n\n**`src/components/AsyncPanel.tsx`**\n- Extracted the 120 ms simulated sync into a shared `schedule(next)` helper backed by a single `timerRef`, plus `clearTimer` for unmount cleanup (preserving the original cleanup behavior).\n- The mount effect still reads `?sync=` once and resolves to `error` or `success` exactly as before, so `/` is unchanged.\n- Added a `Retry sync` button inside the error alert. Its handler immediately sets `loading` and schedules the same 120 ms transition to `success`; it returns early if a timer is already pending, so repeated activation cannot create overlapping timers. The button renders only in the `error` state and so disappears on success. No navigation/reload or state reset — the selected task lives outside this component and `window.location` is never touched.\n\n**`src/styles.css`**\n- Added `.sync-retry { justify-self: start; margin-top: 8px; }` so the recovery action sits below the error copy, reusing the existing `button.secondary` style and existing focus-visible outline rules.\n\n**Commands actually run:** `verify_frontend` → `npm run build` (tsc + vite, success) and `npm run test:public` (Playwright, 6/6 passed). No existing tests were modified.\n\n**Remaining risks:** the retry path has no public test (only the success state does), so its behavior is verified by reasoning rather than an automated assertion; if a future test asserts a different delay constant, the shared `SYNC_DELAY` would be the single place to change. The guard relies on React's single-threaded click handling, which is adequate for this \"no overlapping timers\" requirement.","type":"output_text","logprobs":[]}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":"final_answer"}],"timestamp":"2026-11-22T15:50:22.813251+00:00"}],"meta":{"snapshot_version":1,"aid":0,"role":"workflow_agent","model":"deepseek-flash","session_state":{"used_tokens":20986,"context_tokens":5893,"step_count":5,"markup_recovered":0,"recent_call_hashes":["41a19181bbd813f18f2f604051ce7cea","54c6d4923513570e71525b862782cc14","0b2507d4e6e12b98774fdb7da83e9c8c","09c561a451cdcb895ea6db3f6e9aa484","5c759914606bfe0b55e715095739cfed","8f0d9b45b1d9f0950e534f7c51a3dbca","3c45d71dcb1acaddc13d0e86e5418077"],"reads_since_last_edit":0,"has_landed_write":true,"low_yield_since_progress":0,"distinct_evidence_count":7,"scout_ledger":[{"tool":"file_read","target":"src/components/AsyncPanel.tsx","outcome":"hit","snippet":"File: src/components/AsyncPanel.tsx (30 lines total, showing 1-30) 1 import { useEffect, useState } from 'react'; 2 3 type State = 'loading' | 'success' | 'error'; 4 5 export function AsyncPanel() { 6 const [state, setState] = useState<Stat"},{"tool":"file_read","target":"TASK.md","outcome":"hit","snippet":"File: TASK.md (16 lines total, showing 1-16) 1 # T03 — Recoverable asynchronous error state 2 3 Add a recovery action to the remote-sync error state. 4 5 Acceptance criteria: 6 7 - The existing success path at `/` remains unchanged and neve"},{"tool":"file_read","target":"src/styles.css","outcome":"hit","snippet":"File: src/styles.css (71 lines total, showing 1-71) 1 :root { 2 font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", sans-serif; 3 color: #16201d; 4 background: #eef1eb; 5 font-synthesis: none; 6 } 7 "},{"tool":"git_diff","target":"{\"stat_only\": true}","outcome":"hit","snippet":"Status: working tree clean. diff --stat: (no changes)"},{"tool":"file_write","target":"src/components/AsyncPanel.tsx","outcome":"hit","snippet":"Created/wrote src/components/AsyncPanel.tsx (1823 chars)"},{"tool":"file_write","target":"src/styles.css","outcome":"hit","snippet":"Replaced in src/styles.css: 62 chars → 116 chars (content changed)"},{"tool":"verify_frontend","target":"{}","outcome":"hit","snippet":"Exit code: 0 > regression-board-fixture@1.0.0 verify:agent > npm run build && npm run test:public > regression-board-fixture@1.0.0 build > tsc --noEmit && vite build vite v8.3.8 building client environment for production... transforming... "}],"steps_since_progress":0,"wind_down_done":false,"wind_down_attempts":0,"wind_down_token_mark":0,"budget_reserve_consumed":false,"loop_blocked_since_progress":0,"loop_state":{"ver